.Dd January 31, 2026
.Dt PARADOS.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm parados.conf
.Nd configuration file for parados
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file configures
.Xr parados 1 .
.Pp
The file format is line-oriented. Each non-empty,
non-comment line is a key/value pair in the form:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
key=value
.Ed
.Pp
Whitespace around keys and values ignored.
Lines beginning with
.Sq #
are comments and are ignored.
Unknown keys are ignored but logged.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/parados.conf
System-wide configuration file.
.It Pa ./parados.conf
Fallback configuration file in the current working
directory.
.El
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic media_dir
Directory containing all media files. The library is built
by recursively scanning this directory at startup.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
media_dir=/path/to/media
.Ed
.It Ic server_addr
Address to bind the HTTP server to.
Use
.Cm 127.0.0.1
to listen on the local host only. This is recommended if a
web interface is being hosted on the same machine; exposing
the server to the network may unnecessarily increase risk.
Use
.Cm 0.0.0.0
to listen on all IPv4 interfaces.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
server_addr=0.0.0.0
.Ed
.It Ic server_port
TCP port to listen on.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
server_port=8088
.Ed
.It Ic verbose_log
Enable or disable verbose logging.
Accepted values are
.Cm 1 ,
.Cm 0 ,
.Cm true ,
.Cm false ,
.Cm yes ,
and
.Cm no
(case-insensitive).
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
verbose_log=true
.Ed
.It Ic cors_origin
Configure Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) for web
clients.
.Pp
If empty, no CORS headers are sent.
If set to
.Cm * ,
all origins are allowed.
Otherwise, the value is interpreted as a
comma-separated list of allowed origins (clients that can
interact over the web).
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cors_origin=http://127.0.0.1:8000
.Ed
.It Ic http_io_timeout
Maximum number of seconds the server will block on a single
socket read/write operation.
.Pp
This limits how long a client may stall for while sending a
request or receiving a response. If the timeout is exceeded,
the connection is closed.
.Pp
This option is used to protect against stalled or
misbehaving clients. It does not limit the total duration of
a request or stream.
.Pp
Valid values are integers in the range 1 to 300.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
http_io_timeout=5
.Ed
.It Ic max_clients
Maximum number of concurrent client connections.
If the limit is reached, new connections receive a
.Dv 503
response.
.Pp
Valid values are integers in the range 1 to 1024.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
max_clients=64
.Ed
.It Ic auth_delay
Delay (in ms) before returning
.Dv 401 Unauthorized
responses.
.Pp
This can slow down brute force login attempts.
.Pp
Valid values are non-negative integers 0..
.Dv INT_MAX .
A value of
.Cm 0
disables the delay.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
auth_delay=250
.Ed
.El
.Sh AUTHENTICATION
Authentication entries are specified using repeated groups
of the keys
.Ic user ,
.Ic pass ,
and
.Ic allow .
.Pp
If no
.Ic user
entries are present, authentication is disabled and all files are
accessible.
If one or more users are present, HTTP Basic authentication
is required for all requests except
.Pa /ping .
.Pp
Each
.Ic user
starts a new authentication entry. The following
.Ic pass
and
.Ic allow
lines apply to that user until the next
.Ic user
line.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic user
Set the username for a new authentication entry.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
user=glenda
.Ed
.It Ic pass
Set the password for the most recently declared user. If
empty, the account is passwordless and accepts only an empty
password.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pass=secret
.Ed
.It Ic allow
Add an allowed path prefix for the most recently declared
user. Multiple
.Ic allow
directives may be used.
.Pp
A value of
.Cm *
allows all paths. Otherwise, the value must match the
beginning of a file's relative path. Directory boundaries
are respected.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
allow=Media/
allow=Music/
.Ed
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Minimal configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
media_dir=/path/to/media
server_addr=127.0.0.1
server_port=8088
verbose_log=true
cors_origin=
auth_delay=0
.Ed
.Pp
Two users with separate access:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
user=glenda
pass=pass123
allow=Media/
allow=Music/

user=bob
pass=
allow=TV/NBA/
.Ed
.Pp
Single passwordless administrative user with full access:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
user=admin
pass=
allow=*
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr parados 1 ,
.Xr parados 7
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Abhinav Prasai

